\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Downstream Dice (left) against an independent, segmentation-free measurement of texture fidelity (right, NGF gradient-orientation agreement with the source volume) across the rung sequence. The three noise-fill rungs sit flat at the texture floor while their Dice still rises -- those gains come from richer contrast randomization, not texture. Both quantities jump together at the fill swap, which is the step the texture hypothesis predicts.\relax }}{3}{figure.caption.38}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ngf-dose}{{3}{3}{Downstream Dice (left) against an independent, segmentation-free measurement of texture fidelity (right, NGF gradient-orientation agreement with the source volume) across the rung sequence. The three noise-fill rungs sit flat at the texture floor while their Dice still rises -- those gains come from richer contrast randomization, not texture. Both quantities jump together at the fill swap, which is the step the texture hypothesis predicts.\relax }{figure.caption.38}{}}
\newlabel{fig:ngf-dose@cref}{{[figure][3][]3}{[1][3][]3}}
